WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:04.443
Some Orchard Core features need other features to work.

00:00:04.443 --> 00:00:09.016
In this video, you see how the Features page shows these dependencies, what

00:00:09.016 --> 00:00:13.249
happens to related features when you enable or disable one, and why a

00:00:13.249 --> 00:00:15.620
few features have no working switch.

00:00:20.220 --> 00:00:22.639
A feature can build on other features.

00:00:22.639 --> 00:00:27.752
Users Registration, for example, lets visitors sign up and confirm their email address,

00:00:27.752 --> 00:00:29.731
so it needs the Email feature.

00:00:29.731 --> 00:00:32.700
The features that it needs are its dependencies.

00:00:33.450 --> 00:00:35.955
Orchard Core keeps both sides consistent.

00:00:35.955 --> 00:00:39.686
When you enable a feature, its dependencies are enabled with it.

00:00:39.686 --> 00:00:44.270
When you disable a feature, the features that depend on it are disabled with it.

00:00:48.526 --> 00:00:52.958
The Features page is under Tools, Features, and lists the features of the

00:00:52.958 --> 00:00:54.754
site, grouped by category.

00:00:54.754 --> 00:00:57.110
Let's search for Users Registration.

00:00:57.110 --> 00:01:01.150
The search narrows the list as you type, and matches the name, the

00:01:01.150 --> 00:01:03.956
identifier and the description of a feature.

00:01:04.412 --> 00:01:09.079
The row shows the name of the feature, its identifier, its description, and

00:01:09.079 --> 00:01:10.692
whether it is enabled.

00:01:10.692 --> 00:01:13.804
The badges beside the name are its dependencies:

00:01:13.804 --> 00:01:15.072
Email and Users.

00:01:15.524 --> 00:01:20.174
Point at a badge, and a tooltip shows the description of that dependency.

00:01:20.174 --> 00:01:25.824
The Email badge, for example, describes the infrastructure for configuring email settings.

00:01:26.293 --> 00:01:31.679
The button with three dots, Show indirect dependencies, adds the features that the

00:01:31.679 --> 00:01:33.638
dependencies need in turn:

00:01:33.638 --> 00:01:36.393
here, Roles Core Services and Settings.

00:01:40.607 --> 00:01:42.373
Let's search for email.

00:01:42.373 --> 00:01:47.427
Email is disabled on this site, and so is Users Registration, which needs it.

00:01:47.878 --> 00:01:50.311
Select Enable on Users Registration.

00:01:50.311 --> 00:01:52.917
Enabling does not ask for confirmation.

00:01:52.917 --> 00:01:58.418
A message confirms that the feature was enabled, and it names only the feature you chose.

00:01:58.869 --> 00:02:00.546
Search for email again.

00:02:00.546 --> 00:02:03.958
Email is enabled too, although you did not select it.

00:02:03.958 --> 00:02:08.469
Dependencies that were already enabled, such as Users, stay as they are.

00:02:12.658 --> 00:02:14.319
Let's go the other way.

00:02:14.319 --> 00:02:18.558
Search for email again, and select Disable on Email, the dependency.

00:02:19.018 --> 00:02:21.091
A dialog asks you to confirm.

00:02:21.091 --> 00:02:25.059
It lists the dependent features that are disabled with Email:

00:02:25.059 --> 00:02:26.895
here, Users Registration.

00:02:26.895 --> 00:02:31.278
A feature without enabled dependents only asks whether you are sure.

00:02:31.736 --> 00:02:32.810
Select Yes.

00:02:32.810 --> 00:02:38.494
The message names Email, but a search for registration shows that Users Registration

00:02:38.494 --> 00:02:40.136
is disabled as well.

00:02:44.369 --> 00:02:46.138
Some features are on demand:

00:02:46.138 --> 00:02:49.261
they are turned on only when other features need them.

00:02:49.261 --> 00:02:51.187
The list hides them by default.

00:02:51.187 --> 00:02:54.259
Open the Visibility filter, and clear Hide on demand.

00:02:54.729 --> 00:02:56.871
Search for Roles Core Services.

00:02:56.871 --> 00:03:00.576
Features such as Users need it, so it is enabled for them.

00:03:00.576 --> 00:03:05.266
Its Disable button is inactive, and the tooltip says the feature is enabled

00:03:05.266 --> 00:03:07.639
automatically, based on dependency.

00:03:08.096 --> 00:03:10.342
Some features are always enabled.

00:03:10.342 --> 00:03:15.812
Clear Hide always enabled, and search for the Features feature, the one behind this page.

00:03:15.812 --> 00:03:20.476
Its tooltip says that it is always enabled and cannot be manually disabled.

00:03:22.076 --> 00:03:26.328
To sum up, an on demand feature is enabled while another feature needs

00:03:26.328 --> 00:03:28.454
it, and disabled when none does.

00:03:28.454 --> 00:03:30.748
An always enabled feature stays on.

00:03:30.748 --> 00:03:32.706
Neither has a working switch.

00:03:34.706 --> 00:03:37.598
That's how dependencies work on the Features page:

00:03:37.598 --> 00:03:42.503
enabling a feature enables what it needs, and disabling a feature disables what needs it.

00:03:42.503 --> 00:03:43.846
Thanks for watching.

